                <pb facs="0654" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/3281: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-22T09:00:00-05:00">June 22, 1932—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. Congress yesterday passed administration measure suspending constitutional
                    guarantees for 1 year and authorizing the Executive to extend suspension for
                    additional 2 years if necessary. The apparent purpose of the measure is to serve
                    notice on the opposition that the Machado Government intends to continue to
                    proceed with a strong hand.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
